WEBVTT

00:19:28.655 --> 00:19:31.851
because the economics,
the energy density, are so different

00:19:31.875 --> 00:19:33.289
than nuclear as we know it.

00:19:33.313 --> 00:19:34.775
CA: So to understand it right,

00:19:34.799 --> 00:19:37.081
this involves building
deep into the ground,

00:19:37.105 --> 00:19:42.665
almost like a vertical column
of nuclear fuel, of this spent uranium,

00:19:42.689 --> 00:19:45.829
and then the process starts
at the top and kind of works down?

00:19:45.853 --> 00:19:47.030
BG: That's right.

00:19:47.054 --> 00:19:49.113
Today, you're always
refueling the reactor,

00:19:49.137 --> 00:19:52.329
so you have lots of people and lots
of controls that can go wrong,

00:19:52.353 --> 00:19:55.092
where you're opening it up
and moving things in and out --

00:19:55.116 --> 00:19:57.273
that's not good.

00:19:57.297 --> 00:19:58.470
So if you have very --

00:19:58.494 --> 00:19:59.583
(Laughter)

00:19:59.607 --> 00:20:02.354
very cheap fuel
that you can put 60 years in --